---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const linkClass =
  "text-primary underline decoration-border underline-offset-2 transition-colors duration-150 hover:text-primary-hover";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Sale · Gerfaut Premium"
  description="The terms of sale of Gerfaut Premium: seller, plans and prices, your key, payment in bitcoin, withdrawal, data, liability and applicable law."
>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 md:px-6">
      <article class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <h1
          class="font-display text-[2rem] leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-[2.5rem]"
        >
          Terms of Sale
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
          Gerfaut Premium &middot; Last updated
          <time datetime="2026-09-05">5 September 2026</time>
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 text-h2 font-display">1. Seller</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Gerfaut Premium is sold by Loïc Morel, sole trader (entreprise
          individuelle) registered in France and trading as Pandul. Contact:
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>.
          VAT is not applicable under article 293 B of the French General Tax
          Code (CGI).
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">2. What you buy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Prepaid time on the Gerfaut alert service, tied to an account key.
          From our server, the service watches the Bitcoin wallets you
          register and notifies you through the channels you choose (ntfy,
          Telegram, e-mail, webhook), plus the other Premium services listed
          on the Premium page as they become available. A webhook must point
          at a host the internet can reach: the server refuses a private or
          local address. It is a monitoring service: it never holds keys or
          funds and cannot move them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">3. Plans and prices</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          1 month: 5&nbsp;€. 6 months: 24&nbsp;€. 1 year: 36&nbsp;€. Prices
          are in euro and paid in bitcoin at the rate shown at checkout. A
          launch offer, when displayed, applies to the plan it names. Paid
          time adds to the end of the time you already have.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">4. Your key</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          The account key is shown once, at checkout, before you pay. It is
          the only way to use the time you bought. We store only a hash of it
          and cannot recover, reset or re-issue a lost key. Anyone holding the
          key can use the account. Keep it like a password.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">5. Payment</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Payments go through our own Bark Pay instance and settle on Bitcoin
          (Ark, Lightning or on-chain). Time is credited when the payment is
          confirmed. An underpaid charge is not credited until it is topped
          up; the checkout page shows the remaining amount. An overpayment is
          treated as paid and the difference is not refunded.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">6. Withdrawal</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Within 14 days of purchase you may withdraw by writing to
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>
          with your key: we refund the unused days pro rata, in bitcoin, to
          the address you give us. After 14 days, prepaid time is not
          refundable, except as stated in section 9.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">
          7. What the service can and cannot do
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Alerts are sent as fast as the Bitcoin network and our servers
          allow, usually within seconds. We do not guarantee delivery time or
          availability; incidents are published on
          <a href="https://status.gerfaut-wallet.com" class={linkClass}
            >status.gerfaut-wallet.com</a
          >. The service does not prevent theft and cannot guarantee that
          every movement is detected: network, channel or server outages
          happen. Use it as one layer among others. Nothing here is financial
          advice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">8. Your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          We store the descriptors you register, the addresses derived from
          them, the coins and movements seen on them, the channels you add,
          and the hash of your key. We store no name, no e-mail unless you add
          one as a channel, no IP address and no request logs. Stopping the
          watch on a wallet, or removing a watched wallet from the app,
          deletes its data on the server. The server deletes everything it
          holds under a key 90 days after the paid time on that key runs
          out; a key that was never paid for is deleted 30 days after it was
          created. To delete everything now, use "Forget this key" in the
          app, which offers to delete your data on the server as well, or
          write to
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>
          with your key. We operate the servers ourselves, in Canada and
          France. The data controller is Loïc Morel.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">
          9. Changes and discontinuation
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          We may change or discontinue a service with 30 days' notice on the
          status page. If we discontinue the alert service, unused time is
          refunded pro rata in bitcoin on request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">10. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Do not register wallets you have no right to monitor. One key
          watches up to 21 wallets and may send 60 requests per minute; the
          server refuses what goes past that with a clear error. We may stop
          serving a key that abuses the service.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">11. Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          To the extent the law allows, our liability is limited to the
          amount you paid in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here
          excludes liability that cannot be excluded under French consumer
          law.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">12. Law and disputes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          French law applies. You may bring a dispute to a consumer mediator;
          the mediator's details are available on request at
          <a href="mailto:info@pandul.fr" class={linkClass}>info@pandul.fr</a>.
          EU consumers may also use the
          <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr" class={linkClass}
            >European online dispute resolution platform</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-h2 font-display">13. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Changes are posted on this page with their date. The terms in force
          when you paid apply to that purchase.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
